{# VARIANT v1_verdict_hard — 9B-targeted verdict (anti-discount).

   v1_verdict lifted the 9B 4→77% but left a ~23% residual where it acknowledges
   "threshold met" then DISCOUNTS the evidence's validity ("not definitive… could
   be a memory error") and skips anyway. This variant keeps v1's rendered verdict
   and makes the eject side as HARD and discount-proof as the skip side: when the
   verdict permits ejection it is a MUST, and re-litigating whether the suspicion
   is "definitive" is explicitly disallowed (the score already weighs evidence
   quality). The compliant 9B follows hard commands (it obeys hard-SKIP) — so a
   symmetric hard-EJECT should close the residual. False-eject stays guarded:
   below-threshold still renders MUST-SKIP.
#}
