## Decision rules

1. **Gate verdict — already computed for you, do not recompute.** Your maximum
   suspicion is **{{ "%.2f"|format(_max) }}**; the threshold is **{{ "%.2f"|format(_thr) }}**.
   {% if _max >= _thr %}**{{ "%.2f"|format(_max) }} ≥ {{ "%.2f"|format(_thr) }} — you MUST vote to eject; you may NOT skip.** Set `target` to the living player with the highest suspicion / strongest case. The suspicion score **already weighs how good the evidence is**, so do NOT skip on the grounds that the evidence is "not definitive", "circumstantial", or "could be a memory error" — those are exactly the cases the threshold is built for. A met threshold means you VOTE. Skipping now is a rule violation.{% else %}**{{ "%.2f"|format(_max) }} < {{ "%.2f"|format(_thr) }} — you MUST set `target` to `"SKIP"`.** No candidate crosses the threshold.{% endif %}
2. **Pick the strongest case** among the above-threshold players (if more than one),
   using the transcript and contradiction flags. Do not re-open the gate decision —
   it is already made above.
3. **`primary_reason_id`** references the `MeetingTurn` id{% if transcript.turns %} (e.g.
